---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Docs — Torana">
  <article class="frame prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Documentation</p>
    <h1 class="display">Get Torana running.</h1>
    <p>Start with one request through the proxy. Then add a plugin, connect your coding agent, or dig into how the pieces work.</p>
    <h2>For operators</h2>
    <table><tbody>
      <tr><th><a href="/how-it-works/">How it works</a></th><td>Follow a request through routing, plugin hooks, permissions, and the local controls.</td></tr>
      <tr><th><a href="/quickstart/">Quickstart</a></th><td>Install, configure one provider, and route a harness.</td></tr>
      <tr><th><a href="/docs/support/">Support matrix</a></th><td>Exact provider endpoints, harness paths, cache behavior, and SDK maturity.</td></tr>
      <tr><th><a href="/plugins/">Plugin registry</a></th><td>Pick a plugin, inspect its permissions, and copy its install command.</td></tr>
      <tr><th><a href="/docs/plugin-installation/">Plugin installation</a></th><td>Understand source builds, permissions, and digest approval.</td></tr>
      <tr><th><a href="https://github.com/torana-edge/torana-edge/blob/main/docs/QUICKSTART.md#configure">Configuration ↗</a></th><td>Seed versus managed configuration, providers, authentication, and routing.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <h2>For plugin authors</h2>
    <table><tbody>
      <tr><th><a href="https://github.com/torana-edge/torana-plugin-sdk">SDK repository ↗</a></th><td>Go and Rust helpers, templates, tests, and the interface between Torana and compiled plugins.</td></tr>
      <tr><th><a href="https://github.com/torana-edge/torana-plugins">Official plugins ↗</a></th><td>Reviewed source examples with versioned manifests.</td></tr>
      <tr><th><a href="https://github.com/torana-edge/torana-plugin-sdk/tree/main/proto/torana/v1">Protocol reference ↗</a></th><td>Message definitions exchanged between Torana and its WASM plugins.</td></tr>
      <tr><th><a href="/plugins/submit/">Share a plugin</a></th><td>Keep your plugin in your own repository and request a catalogue listing.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </article>
</Layout>
